{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773084679,"nonce":"gc6OvI1sps+g4PIWPMMmLtuQdmQ=","title":"GraphView: top-level operational graph of issues, branches, auth requests, sessions","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd a top-level GraphView page to the Mandible dashboard — a dedicated navigation and monitoring surface that visualizes the operational state of the system as a graph. Accessible via a round icon button in the nav bar (to the left of the gear button), styled consistently with the gear icon button.\n\n## Entities as nodes\n\n- **Issues** (git-bug): labeled by type (umbrella, error, feature, deferred), colored by status\n- **Branches**: with lineage edges to parent branches\n- **Auth requests**: connected to their head branch and to linked issues (via `Bug:` trailer parsing)\n- **Sessions**: with parent→child edges for subagent trees; linked to issues via session_issues\n- Possible future: conversations as leaf nodes attached to sessions\n\n## Edges\n\n- Umbrella → child issue (requires server-side parsing of issue description text and labels — see also #f7c65e4 for issue cross-reference syntax)\n- Session → issue (session_issues join table, already exists)\n- Auth request → branch (head_branch / base_branch fields)\n- Auth request → issue (Bug: trailer in commit_message — currently UI-only, needs server-side extraction)\n- Session → session (parent_id, already exists)\n- Branch → issue (Bug: trailers in last_commit_message — needs server-side extraction)\n\n## New server-side work required\n\n- `GET /api/graph` endpoint that joins across all entity types and returns typed `{ nodes, edges }` payload\n- Bug: trailer parsing moved server-side (currently only in auth.tsx UI code)\n- Umbrella/child relationship inference from issue labels + description parsing\n- branch→issue edge construction from last_commit_message Bug: refs\n\n## Filtering and display\n\n- **Default view**: last 50 events or last 3 days (whichever is smaller), open issues only, closed/merged hidden by toggle\n- **Real-time adjustable**: recency slider or date picker in the view toolbar\n- **Repo + branch filtering**: same filtering pattern as other tabs, sourced from the work repo registry (NOT string-parsed from git paths — must use the canonical repo identity from the registry to avoid the branch-name-as-repo-name bug)\n- **Live updates**: subscribe to existing SSE events (session:*, auth:*, work:branch:*) to animate node state changes in real time\n\n## Rendering\n\n- D3 (SVG-based) — not Sigma/WebGL. Node count with default filtering is 30-80; D3 SVG is sufficient and gives CSS-driven styling for visual differentiation and animation.\n- Visually specialized node types: agents/sessions should look distinctive (pulsing when active?), auth requests should convey urgency state, issues should convey label/status at a glance\n- Click node → navigate to that entity's primary tab, pre-filtered (hash deep-link)\n- Hover → tooltip with key fields\n\n## Navigation topology note\n\nIssues currently have one outbound navigable link (→ sessions). Issue→auth and issue→branch connections exist in the data but are not surfaced in the UI. The graph view will be the first place these connections are made visible. See #f7c65e4 for the cross-reference rendering work.\n\n## Nav placement\n\nRound icon button to the left of the gear button in the header. Same visual style as the gear button. Does NOT go in the overflow menu. Its own tab entry in the Route union.\n\n## Related issues\n\n- #f7c65e4 — issue cross-reference syntax (#id → hyperlinks), prerequisite for navigable issue→issue edges\n- cf51a72 (HumbleB) — specialized visual representation brainstorm, future integration consideration","files":null}]}